Well, that means a factor of 3 or 4 for the number of games to play. For
me that "chance for a bones" would make any effort (like this trap-setup
achievement) uninteresting. But if that player can't win the game (or is
so bored about constantly winning?) it may be the only interesting "job"
he can think of that satisfies him; maybe like boys in the sandbox who
like destroying the sandcastle of others? (Psychologically nothing new.)
Yes, at some point they might get bored (or grow up), but who knows.

That said; on the other hand, the deliberate deployment of such traps,
*could* also become something interesting; to create a challenge or a
puzzle for experienced player to solve. It should run on some dedicated
server, of course. And the Nethack code should be adapted to allow a more
controlled creation of such bones, or, respectively, a detached challenge
generator via bones files might even be better suited.

In the past I occasionally had very difficult bones levels[*]; ignoring
any insta-death situations, handling such levels was mostly interesting.

